{"id": "EUVD-2026-104293", "enisaUuid": "f1b79e61-4d1d-3a10-9443-7c16ccc55fe0", "description": "libaribb24 (aribb24) through 1.0.3 contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in src/parser.c that allows attackers to corrupt heap memory via an oversized caption data unit. Attackers can supply a crafted caption PES packet in a media file or broadcast stream, processed through arib_parse_pes(), to crash FFmpeg or VLC and possibly corrupt further memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:34:41", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/aribb24-caption-data-unit-and-csi-oob-write", "https://github.com/nkoriyama/aribb24/blob/v1.0.3/src/parser.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libaribb24-aribb24-through-1.0.3-heap-buffer-overflow-via-parse-data-unit-statement-body"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pgf4-9h53-rfcj", "CVE-2026-112280"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "45e93c1c-9334-3023-9572-0a4df6b3a475", "product": {"name": "aribb24", "vendor": {"name": "nkoriyama"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e116fa9b-f275-3b06-b2fa-6a7951a679ea", "vendor": {"name": "nkoriyama"}}], "isExploited": false}